        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "•Coonan Property present a spacious, approx. 201 sq.m, four-bedroom semi-detached family home with a fully self-contained one-bedroom annexe, right in the heart of Celbridge\n•Situated in the highly sought-after The Grove` residential development, this impressive and versatile home offers an exceptional combination of spacious accommodation, superb flexibility and an enviable location just 300m from Celbridge Main Street.\n•Ideal for modern family living, the main house offers generous, well-proportioned accommodation over two floors. Upstairs are three spacious double bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite, together with a family bathroom. The ground floor offers further versatility with a fourth double bedroom/study, a bright south-facing living room with open fire, and a spacious open-plan kitchen, living and dining area with patio doors opening onto the south-facing rear garden ideal for family life and entertaining. A guest W.C. and large integral garage complete the accommodation, providing valuable additional space and potential for a variety of uses.\n•A standout feature is the fully self-contained one-bedroom annexe, with its own private entrance, kitchen/living area, double bedroom and bathroom. Ideal for multi-generational living, independent accommodation for family or guests, a home office, or as an attractive rental opportunity.\n•To the rear is a sunny south-facing garden with mature pear trees, while the generous front driveway provides off-street parking for two cars and potential for more if required.\n•The property is ready to move into and enjoy immediately, while also offering excellent scope to modernise and create a home tailored to the purchaser`s own style and needs.\n•The location is a real highlight. The Grove is a mature, attractive and beautifully landscaped development, offering a peaceful residential setting while being within an easy stroll of everything Celbridge has to offer. Celbridge Main Street is just minutes away, with a wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and everyday amenities close at hand. The beautiful Castletown House and Demesne is also within walking distance, providing an exceptional amenity on the doorstep.\n•For commuters, the property is ideally positioned for the N4/M4 motorway network, with regular bus services to Dublin city centre and Hazelhatch train station within easy reach.\n•A rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family home with an exceptional degree of flexibility, a south-facing garden and a truly convenient town-centre location.\n\n\nGuide Price\n545,000\n\nType of Transaction\nPrivate Treaty\n\n4 Bedroom House:\n\nDriveway \nTo the front, an extensive driveway provides off-street parking for two cars, with a front lawn.\n\nEntrance Porch 2.63m x 2.48m\nTiled floor, light fitting, part-glazed door to the front and a further door through to the entrance hallway, forming a separate porch area.\n\nEntrance Hallway 5.16m x 2.28m\nOak floor, coving, light fitting and useful storage under the stairs. Elegant wooden staircase with carpet runner rising to the second landing.\n\nGuest W.C. 0.96m x 1.64m\nOak floor, w.c., w.h.b., window and light fitting.\n\nLiving Room 4.98m x 3.33m\nSouth facing room to the rear of the house, overlooking the garden with open fire and solid oak floor, coving, curtain pole and light fitting.\n\nKitchen 5.58m x 2.72m\nSouth facing to the rear of the house. Fitted wooden kitchen floor and wall units, tiled splashback, stainless steel sink and two light fittings. Fully plumbed, with double oven, hob and integrated fridge freezer. Lino floor covering,\n\nDining Room 2.76m x 4.96m\nSouth facing with a double sliding door out to the rear garden and a further door to the covered side access & garage area. Lino floor covering, two light fittings\n\nBedroom 4/Study 3.31m x 3.10m\nDouble bedroom/study to the front of the house, light fitting, carpeted floor.\n\nSide Access (Garage to Rear Garden) 1.14m x 5.26m\nConcrete floor providing covered access from the garage through to the rear garden.\n\nGarage 5.00m x 2.93m\nConcrete floor, roller shutter door and light fitting.\n\nLanding 2.64m x 1.34m\nOak floor, coving, light fitting, hotpress and access to the attic (with fitted ladder).\n\nMaster Bedroom 4.36m x 3.26m\nSouth facing double room, Oak floor, light fitting.\n\nEnsuite 0.95m x 2.37m\nTiled and part-tiled floor and walls, shower cubicle, w.c., w.h.b., extractor fan and light fitting.\n\nBedroom 2 5.10m x 2.82m\nSouth facing double room, oak floor, light fitting.\n\nBedroom 3 3.14m x 3.31m\nFront facing double room, oak floor, light fitting.\n\nBathroom 2.43m x 1.84m\nTiled floor, part-tiled walls, bath, w.c., w.h.b. and radiator.\n\nSelf-Contained Annexe:\n\nA fully self-contained unit to the side of the property with its own separate entrance and stairs.\n\nEntrance Hall 1.28m x 1.05m \nTimber floor with stairs and carpet runner rising to the second landing.\nLanding 2.10m x 1.67m\nSolid pine floor.\nKitchen/Living Room 4.59m x 4.09m \nSolid pine floor with tiled flooring to the kitchen area, fitted floor and wall units and stainless steel sink. Fully plumbed, with oven, gas hob, fridge freezer, dishwasher, washing machine and a separate gas boiler.\nBedroom 3.65m x 4.08m \nSouth facing double room, solid pine floor, double glazed windows to the rear, freestanding wardrobes and coving.\nBathroom 1.90m x 1.75m \nTiled floor, part-tiled walls, shower cubicle with electric shower and mirror, w.c., w.h.b., window, recessed lights and coving.\n\nGarden\nSouth facing rear garden with mature pear trees, a patio area and a block-built shed (housing the heating system), enjoying a good degree of privacy. \n\nAdditional Information:\nGross internal floor area approx. 201 sq.m or 2,163 sq.ft\nBuilt c. late 1970`s\nExtended in late 1980`s\nAccess through garage directly to back garden\nPotential to extend the front driveway into lawn space\nPositioned beside a well maintained green area\nJust 5 minutes walk from Celbridge Town centre\n\n\nItems Included in sale:\nDouble oven, hob and integrated fridge freezer in both the house and annex.\n\nServices\nMains water\nOil fired central heating \n\nBER \nC\n\nViewing\nBy appointment only.\n\nEircode: W23 R981\n\nContact Information\nSales Person \nMick Wright \n016288400\n"
      },
